{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Get details for one Sentry alert rule by ID or exact name.\n\nUse this tool when you need to inspect an alert rule's exact conditions, query, triggers, and actions before explaining or planning changes.\nTo list or search alert rules, use find_alert_rules instead.\n\n<examples>\nget_alert_rule(organizationSlug='my-org', kind='metric', ruleIdOrName='12345')\nget_alert_rule(organizationSlug='my-org', kind='issue', projectSlug='backend', ruleIdOrName='Notify backend team')\nget_alert_rule(organizationSlug='my-org', projectSlug='backend', ruleIdOrName='P95 latency')\n</examples>\n\n<hints>\n- Prefer get_metric_monitor_details for Metric Monitors. With kind=metric, numeric IDs retain their legacy alert-rule meaning; detector:123 explicitly identifies monitor 123.\n- With `kind='all'`, a digit-only `ruleIdOrName` is treated as an exact alert rule name.\n- Issue Alerts are notification workflows and may cover multiple projects or have no connected sources. Omit projectSlug to inspect organization-wide.\n- Issue details include complete conditions, notification actions, connected monitors and project scope. Inaccessible or session-restricted sources are marked explicitly.\n</hints>","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"fresh":{"description":"Bypass cached reads.","type":"boolean"},"kind":{"default":"all","description":"Which alert family to inspect. Numeric metric IDs are legacy alert-rule IDs, not monitor IDs. `all` performs an exact-name lookup.","enum":["all","issue","metric"],"type":"string"},"organizationSlug":{"description":"The organization's slug. You can find a existing list of organizations you have access to using the `find_organizations()` tool.","type":"string"},"projectSlug":{"anyOf":[{"description":"The project's slug, or exact lowercase `all` when a tool supports all-projects scope. Other casing is treated as a project slug.","type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null},"regionUrl":{"anyOf":[{"description":"The region URL for the organization you're querying, if known. For Sentry's Cloud Service (sentry.io), this is typically the region-specific URL like 'https://us.sentry.io'. For self-hosted Sentry installations, this parameter is usually not needed and should be omitted. You can find the correct regionUrl from the organization details using the `find_organizations()` tool.","type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null},"ruleIdOrName":{"description":"An Alert ID or exact name. Metric references accept legacy numeric alert-rule IDs or detector:123 for canonical monitor IDs.","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["ruleIdOrName"],"type":"object"},"name":"get_alert_rule","outputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"alertRule":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Set when the match is an Issue Alert.","properties":{"actionFilters":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"actions":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"config":{"additionalProperties":{},"propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"type":"object"},"data":{"additionalProperties":{},"propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"type":"object"},"id":{"type":["string","number"]},"integrationId":{"type":["string","number","null"]},"status":{"type":"string"},"type":{"type":"string"}},"required":["type","config","data"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"conditions":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"comparison":{},"conditionResult":{},"id":{"type":["string","number"]},"type":{"type":"string"}},"required":["type","comparison","conditionResult"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"id":{"type":["string","number"]},"logicType":{"type":"string"}},"required":["logicType","conditions","actions"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"config":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"frequency":{"type":"number"}}